 Write `~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc`, an always-applied rule that sets pstack's model per role.
 
 ## Steps
+
+### 0. Register the bundled agents
+
+Resolve `scripts/register-agents.mjs` relative to this `SKILL.md` and run it with Node.js using its absolute path. The script locates the agent definitions in this installed plugin, then registers `poteto-agent` and `comment-sicko` under `$CODEX_HOME/agents/`, or `~/.codex/agents/` when `CODEX_HOME` is unset. Users do not need to copy or edit the TOML files themselves.
+
+Read the JSON result and report which agents were installed, updated, or already unchanged. Re-running setup leaves identical files untouched. The registration record tracks the installed file hashes so updates replace only unchanged files previously registered by pstack. If a name conflicts with another file, or a registered file was edited, report the conflict and stop setup; do not overwrite it or change unrelated agent definitions. Registration does not modify `config.toml`, model preferences, or agent instruction bodies.
+
+For an isolated check, pass `--codex-home` with an absolute temporary directory; `--dry-run` previews registration without writing files. Successful registration confirms the files were written, not that this conversation has loaded or executed the agents. Continue with model configuration after registration succeeds.
 
 ### 1. Detect available models
 
diff --git a/skills/setup-pstack/scripts/register-agents.mjs b/skills/setup-pstack/scripts/register-agents.mjs
